      ":question/id": "181e4433-3ec6-547a-9eec-574523bea082",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 4 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:=-2{R}_{3}$ on $A?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{3}:=-2{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $-2.$\n\nMultiplying the third row by $-2$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 4 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{3}:=-2{R}_{3} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 4 & 7 & -3 \\\\ -2\\cdot (8) & -2\\cdot (6) & -2\\cdot (8)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 4 & 7 & -3 \\\\ -16 & -12 & -16\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
